# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Financial Intelligence Platform — .gitignore
#
# Deliberately short. The official dotnet template is ~350 lines covering
# Xamarin, TFS, ReSharper and other things this repo will never contain.
# Everything here is something this project can actually produce.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- .NET build output -----------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
artifacts/            # .NET 10 unified artifacts output path
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# --- .NET tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
*.user                # per-developer project settings (*.csproj.user etc.)
*.suo
*.userprefs
.dotnet/
project.lock.json
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
msbuild.wrn

# --- Test output -----------------------------------------------------------
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
*.trx
TestResults/

# NOTE: test fixtures ARE committed on purpose.
# tests/**/Fixtures/ holds trimmed CVM DFP/ITR/CAD extracts and B3 COTAHIST
# records so the suite runs offline and a stranger can clone and test with no
# network access at all. Do not add a rule that excludes them.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The data path needs no credentials at all — CVM and B3 are public files. The
# only secret is the development-time cloud AI key (ADR 0006), and it lives in
# dotnet user-secrets or an environment variable. See README "Configuration".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.Secrets.json
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem

# --- Local data ------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres bind-mount volume, if docker-compose.yml uses one instead of a
# named volume.
data/postgres/

# Raw CVM and B3 downloads kept while debugging parsers. The yearly archives are
# large and re-downloadable from the published files, so they stay local. Curated
# fixtures that tests depend on go under tests/**/Fixtures/ and ARE committed.
data/raw/
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Local SQLite scratch databases, if you ever use one to try something out
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Local models ----------------------------------------------------------
# Ollama stores models under ~/.ollama, but guard against anyone pulling a
# GGUF into the repo. A single 8B model is ~5 GB and GitHub will reject it.
models/
*.gguf
*.bin

# --- Editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Rider / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.sln.iml

# Visual Studio
.vs/

# VS Code — ignore personal settings, but commit the shared run configuration
# so a stranger cloning the repo can hit F5 and have it work.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Personal working notes ------------------------------------------------
# AI-assistant instructions and my own session to-do list. Neither is needed to
# build, test or understand the project; docs/ carries the durable reasoning.
CLAUDE.md
NEXT.md
# Build walkthroughs are my own study notes, kept locally.
docs/walkthrough/
docs/superpowers/
.superpowers/
.claude/

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# --- Misc ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
node_modules/         # only if the static frontend ever grows a build step
